{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00022",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 4.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Okay, so hi, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.0,
      "end_seconds": 9.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Yes, come in, take a seat. What can I do for you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.13,
      "end_seconds": 21.6,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got swelling in my left calf. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.46,
      "end_seconds": 24.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.65,
      "end_seconds": 27.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "It's been about a week now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.23,
      "end_seconds": 31.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "And what do you do to cope with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.7,
      "end_seconds": 39.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "Only raising the leg, and it's not much. Oh, and pain in that calf. Had that since last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.39,
      "end_seconds": 52.74,
      "duration_seconds": 12.35,
      "text": "Just so you know how the rest of the visit will go: I'll finish my notes, we'll agree on the plan, and the front desk will help with anything that needs booking. You shouldn't need to chase anything yourself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.55,
      "end_seconds": 59.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Good, I was wondering how this would go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.54,
      "end_seconds": 64.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Have you had any chest pain or recent injury to the leg?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.62,
      "end_seconds": 70.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Yeah, no, no chest pain or recent injury to the leg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.71,
      "end_seconds": 73.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Mm-hm. What about swelling in the other leg?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.39,
      "end_seconds": 78.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "No swelling in the other leg, thank goodness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.7,
      "end_seconds": 92.76,
      "duration_seconds": 14.06,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.43,
      "end_seconds": 95.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.26,
      "end_seconds": 100.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions, anything you've been treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.71,
      "end_seconds": 116.73,
      "duration_seconds": 15.02,
      "text": "I've had high blood pressure for about a year now. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, you know, to be honest. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.21,
      "end_seconds": 121.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.14,
      "end_seconds": 133.5,
      "duration_seconds": 11.36,
      "text": "Right, yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.64,
      "end_seconds": 138.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 139.2,
      "end_seconds": 146.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "I take ramipril, 5 milligrams, every morning for my blood pressure. I'm on paracetamol, 500 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.62,
      "end_seconds": 151.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.56,
      "end_seconds": 154.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.31,
      "end_seconds": 160.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.9,
      "end_seconds": 164.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Dust. I come out in... well, sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.97,
      "end_seconds": 168.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Let me just write this down properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.18,
      "end_seconds": 190.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "That's saved, thanks for waiting. Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 191.41,
      "end_seconds": 192.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.77,
      "end_seconds": 197.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Right, has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.84,
      "end_seconds": 213.84,
      "duration_seconds": 16.0,
      "text": "Not really, uh, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 214.28,
      "end_seconds": 218.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "Alright, have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.67,
      "end_seconds": 233.59,
      "duration_seconds": 13.92,
      "text": "For the most part, um, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.57,
      "end_seconds": 246.96,
      "duration_seconds": 12.39,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.26,
      "end_seconds": 250.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.53,
      "end_seconds": 271.34,
      "duration_seconds": 20.81,
      "text": "From what you've told me, this looks most like a possible deep vein clot. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had swelling in your left calf for about a week, and no chest pain or swelling in the other leg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.55,
      "end_seconds": 274.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.43,
      "end_seconds": 289.69,
      "duration_seconds": 14.26,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.53,
      "end_seconds": 292.76,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.29,
      "end_seconds": 302.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "We should do a D-dimer blood test for suspected DVT. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.07,
      "end_seconds": 304.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.55,
      "end_seconds": 321.9,
      "duration_seconds": 16.35,
      "text": "Keep walking gently, and don't massage the calf. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. If you get chest pain or sudden breathlessness, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. Let's review you after the scan."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 323.24,
      "end_seconds": 327.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.22,
      "text": "Yeah, sure, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.83,
      "end_seconds": 331.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.59,
      "end_seconds": 336.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "So, I come back after the scan. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.82,
      "end_seconds": 342.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.96,
      "end_seconds": 346.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "That's all, thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.5,
      "end_seconds": 349.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "Alright, goodbye."
    }
  ]
}